{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1198673-help-me-reframe-the-talassi","id":1198673,"title":"Help Me Reframe The Talassi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-23T08:27:52-07:00","id":1198673,"title":"Help Me Reframe The Talassi","content":"No, this isn't about their curse.<br /> <br /> It is about the capturing people, though, because to me that seems more like it should be a Hunger than a Family. So I'm wondering how to see it in terms of a Family. Is it the fear of living in a world constrained by others - authority rather than the outsider or face in the crowd the Inguma represent? Or is it a subset of being trapped - should I extend them to burial alive, caves, and getting lost?<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T09:11:52-07:00","id":1198698,"title":"","content":"It's all right there already. Nightmares of Confinement.<br /> <br /> That job you hate, the 9-5 you waste away at every day because the pay is good and the idea that you get to do what you love is a myth? That's Confinement.<br /> The relationship you should have left years ago, but you can't because you have to consider the kids and what's best for them? That's Confinement.<br /> The school you went to, so you could get a 'real job' instead of pursuing your passions? The crushing weight of reality, strangling your dreams before they have a chance to bloom? Confinement.<br /> To your suggestions - being buried alive, trapped in a cave, or even getting lost - all of those can be Confinement.<br /> <br /> To be confined is to be trapped, yes, but it's also to be limited or constrained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:20:04-07:00","id":1198737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1198673-help-me-reframe-the-talassi?p=1198698#post1198698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That job you hate, the 9-5 you waste away at every day because the pay is good and the idea that you get to do what you love is a myth? That's Confinement.<br /> The relationship you should have left years ago, but you can't because you have to consider the kids and what's best for them? That's Confinement.<br /> The school you went to, so you could get a 'real job' instead of pursuing your passions? The crushing weight of reality, strangling your dreams before they have a chance to bloom? Confinement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are good, thanks. So... in the pithy &quot;scary because X&quot; breakdown, they might be scary because you're trapped with them?<br /> <br /> So as well as abducting or imprisoning people, a Talassi might look for ways to trap them in the situations they're in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:36:35-07:00","id":1198741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1198673-help-me-reframe-the-talassi?p=1198737#post1198737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So as well as abducting or imprisoning people, a Talassi might look for ways to trap them in the situations they're in?</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means! Just as other Families might go more metaphorical, Talassi can express their nature that way. They cover a range of fears that previously could (and still can) have been located between hopelessness and drowning, the idea you're stuck somewhere and kept there against your will","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T12:19:55-07:00","id":1198793,"title":"","content":"Hunger is the What; Family is the How.<br /> <br /> A Talassii Tyrant is stereotyped as the stern prison warden, deriving sustenance from the power it wields over those whom it keeps physically trapped in its prison. But it could just as easily be the CEO of a Fortune 500 company, famous for its incredibly low turnover rates - their ironclad contracts prove every bit as confining and unbreakable as the prison's walls.<br /> <br /> A Talassii Enabler can feed through sadistic choices - stick to your morals and suffer the consequences, or transgress and escape. Eat this BLT or starve. Renounce your faith or lose your job. Cheat on your husband or have your previous infidelities exposed. The truly canny Captor will even ensure that no matter <i>what </i>choice the mark makes, they will still Feast.<br /> <br /> A Talassii Collector forces their prey to give up their most prized possession in order to become free. Maybe they trap the person in predatory loans and hidden fees, until they're forced to sell the <i>one thing</i> they promised they'd never party with. Maybe they threaten to release ruinous information unless the person produces whatever matters most to them. The point is that the person is trapped, and the only key is to give it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T13:19:46-07:00","id":1198820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1198673-help-me-reframe-the-talassi?p=1198793#post1198793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Talassii Tyrant is stereotyped as the stern prison warden, deriving sustenance from the power it wields over those whom it keeps physically trapped in its prison. But it could just as easily be the CEO of a Fortune 500 company, famous for its incredibly low turnover rates - their ironclad contracts prove every bit as confining and unbreakable as the prison's walls.<br /> <br /> A Talassii Enabler can feed through sadistic choices - stick to your morals and suffer the consequences, or transgress and escape. Eat this BLT or starve. Renounce your faith or lose your job. Cheat on your husband or have your previous infidelities exposed. The truly canny Captor will even ensure that no matter <i>what </i>choice the mark makes, they will still Feast.<br /> <br /> A Talassii Collector forces their prey to give up their most prized possession in order to become free. Maybe they trap the person in predatory loans and hidden fees, until they're forced to sell the <i>one thing</i> they promised they'd never party with. Maybe they threaten to release ruinous information unless the person produces whatever matters most to them. The point is that the person is trapped, and the only key is to give it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great! Thankyou so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}